    "https://jobs.plattsburgh.edu/postings/11399": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Environmental Science",
      "description": "SUNY College at Plattsburgh Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty, Environmental Science Skip to Main Content SUNY Plattsburgh > Human Resources Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Notice of Non-Discrimination Pay Equity Executive Order Return to Human Resources Services Adjunct Faculty, Environmental Science Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this ATR Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications begins immediately and continues on a periodic basis. Please submit resume/CV, cover letter, any available teaching evaluations, and contact information for 3 current references. Official transcripts from an accredited institution will be required prior to employment. ATR Details Position Details Search Number PJ # 5006L Title Adjunct Faculty, Environmental Science Category Part-Time Faculty Department Earth & Environmental Science About The Position: The Center for Earth and Environmental Science at SUNY Plattsburgh is seeking qualified individuals to teach courses in Environmental Science. Potential openings may include courses in Environmental Planning, general Ecology labs and Geographic Information Systems. Successful candidates will be committed to excellence in teaching in an institution dedicated primarily to undergraduate education. They will be expected to demonstrate an understanding of and sensitivity to diversity and gender issues, as SUNY Plattsburgh is committed to ensuring that its graduates are educated to succeed in an increasingly complex, multicultural, and interdependent wor